    "President Prabowo Subianto held a meeting with ten former National Police chiefs at his residence in Hambalang.",
    "Minister of Home Affairs Tito Karnavian stated that discussions focused on addressing state leakage and national security concerns.",
    "The former police leaders expressed their support for the current government's efforts regarding law enforcement and national policy."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "President Prabowo Subianto recently convened a group of ten former Indonesian National Police (Kapolri) chiefs at his residence in Hambalang, Bogor. The meeting, which included Minister of Home Affairs Tito Karnavian, was held to facilitate high-level communication between the current administration and past law enforcement leadership. According to officials, the primary agenda item was the issue of state leakage, a term used to describe systemic losses of national resources or revenue. This gathering took place during a period of heightened public attention regarding law enforcement and regulatory scrutiny. Reports indicate that the former police officials collectively affirmed their backing for the government's ongoing initiatives and broader law enforcement agendas. The event has drawn significant media coverage, with authorities clarifying that the meeting served to align leadership perspectives on critical administrative and state-level challenges facing the administration.",
